  "report_week": "5",
  "report_period": "Week 5 (23rd Jan to 30th Jan 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Minoa Marine have committed their Kamsarmax \"Aya\" 83/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 10,8 mill. Remind you that back in November, the sister vessel \"Yasa Pioneer\" 82/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026) was sold at USD 10,7 mill. Furthermore, the \"Cretansea\" 81/2009 Universal, Japan (SS 03/2029, DD 03/2027) was committed to Greek interests at USD 15,15 mill. Note that the two-years- younger sister vessel \"Key Frontier\" 80/2011 Universal, Japan (SS 06/2030, DD 05/2028) was sold in December at high USD 18 mill. Minoa Marine have also committed their Panamax \"Anthea\" 76/2006 Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) at USD 9,7 mill, while the sister vessel \"Sfera\" 76/2006 Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026) was sold in December at USD 8,75 mill. Moreover, the younger \"Global Bonanza\" 74/2011 Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) was committed to Greek interests at USD 15,3 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"KT Birdie\" 74/2011 Sasebo, Japan (SS 10/2030, DD 08/2028) was committed a week ago at USD 16,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Costamare have committed their \"Clara\" 56/2008 IHI, Japan (SS 06/2028, DD 09/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 11,8 mill. Remind you that the \"Vega Stetind\" 55/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS 02/2028, DD 12/2025) was committed back in November at USD 11 mill. In addition, following the sale of the \"Spar Taurus\" 53/2005 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 11/2025) back in September at USD 8,8 mill, Spar Shipping have now committed the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Spar Canis\" 53/2006 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 03/2026) to Chinese interests at rgn USD 9 mill. The Handysize \"Jetstream\" 34/2012 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 05/2027) was committed to undisclosed interests at rgn USD 13,5 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Aphrodite M\" 34/2011 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 10/2026) was sold in December at USD 12,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Following the acquisition of the Suezmax resales \"North Star\" & \"Viking Start\" 157/2026 Daehan, Korea (Scrubber fitted) back in November at USD 97 mill each from Atlas Maritime, Okeanis Eco Tankers have now purchased two more sister resales, the \"Arctic Star\" & \"Tromso Star\" 156/2026 Daehan, Korea (Scrubber fitted) at USD 99,3 mill each. The LR1 \"Hafnia Shinano\" 76/2008 Dalian, China (SS 10/2028, DD 01/2027) was committed at USD 15 mill. Note that earlier this month, the sister vessel \"Pelagic Tope\" 76/2008 Dalian, China (SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026, DPP) was sold at USD 13,8 mill. The MR2 \"Star Merlin\" 53/2007 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS/DD 02/2027) was committed at USD 14,4 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Okee Ulf\" 53/2006 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 11/2030, DD 12/2028) was committed a week ago at USD 12,9 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 6,000/8,000 pd range. Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/17,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South Africa into India were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 15,000/18,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 23,000/25,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into South East Asia were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 23,000/24,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into China were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K/800K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 17,500 pd for 11/13 months employment basis delivery Japan.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 6,000/8,000 pd range. Indonesian trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 7,000/9,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips via Arabian Gulf into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 110K/120K. West African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Trips from US Gulf into East Africa were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/600K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from South East Asia via Australia into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. US Gulf coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into East Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
